OL,3,GNEWSARoute linking town centre and rail
OL,4,Astation approved
OL,5,
OL,6,FA #6.9m travel corridor which will link
OL,7,Fa town centre to its new train station
OL,8,Fhas been approved.
OL,10,FThe route, in Blyth, will pass
OL,11,Femployment sites and schools as it
OL,12,Flinks the town centre with Blyth
OL,13,FBebside rail station.
OL,15,FIt will run along residential streets
OL,16,Fto the south of Cowpen Road and aims to
OL,17,Fboost walking and cycling options.
OL,19,FAbout #4.8m of the scheme is funded via
OL,20,Fexternal grants, according to the Local
OL,21,FDemocracy Reporting Service.
